//
// Scoping decision: pt-BR's affix rules are far more generative than
// pt-PT's (allowing deep stacking of prefixes and superlative suffixes,
// e.g. "sesquiinternacionalizabilissimamente"), which would have produced
// an unreasonably bloated ~11.9M-word dictionary dominated by obscure
// derivational curiosities rather than words a player would plausibly
// encounter. Instead: pt-PT's full expansion (2,679,157 words, capped at
// 15 letters -- the maximum a Scrabble board can hold, same cap used for
// Polish) forms the deep tier, and only pt-BR's own dictionary headwords
// not already covered by pt-PT (206,641 words) were added as
// Brazilian-specific extras, rather than pt-BR's full mechanical
// expansion. Final scope: 2,885,798 words before merging with the
// existing cleaned base.
//
